&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote position open to candidates residing in the US. Relocation assistance will not be provided for this role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Americas Field Activation &amp;amp; Execution team, defining and executing the strategy for field-specific enablement needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of global skill programs across the field (roughly 70% of the team&#39;s focus), while addressing bespoke, sales-team-specific enablement needs (roughly 20%) and stakeholder engagement (roughly 10%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage quarterly enablement &amp;amp; leadership team connects to align on business impact and emerging needs with sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide structured feedback to the global program teams to ensure global programs meet specific field team needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop your team of field enablement managers, building organizational depth and bench strength.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion, role model, and embed Samsara&#39;s operating principles as we scale our enablement programs globally and across new offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience, including 7+ years in sales as a quota-carrying Account Executive or sales manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a field-facing enablement or sales operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of driving adoption of programs across a distributed sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management skills, with experience aligning field needs with global program teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to influence senior sales leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
